1
00:00:02,741 --> 00:00:04,613
[indistinct radio chatter]

2
00:00:06,136 --> 00:00:08,051
[sirens wailing in distance]

3
00:00:10,401 --> 00:00:12,577
Excuse me.
Can I get a comment, please?

4
00:00:18,322 --> 00:00:21,369
Yes, ma'am,
keep it right back here.

5
00:00:21,456 --> 00:00:23,327
[helicopter flying overhead]

6
00:00:26,722 --> 00:00:29,246
- Captain.
- Agent Lisbon.

7
00:00:29,333 --> 00:00:31,031
Don't think
we'll be needing you guys.

8
00:00:31,118 --> 00:00:33,207
'We like the neighbor kid
who found the body.'

9
00:00:33,294 --> 00:00:36,036
- Did he confess?
- Ah, he's a real squirrel.

10
00:00:36,123 --> 00:00:38,081
- Did you kill her?
- Did you kill her?

11
00:00:38,168 --> 00:00:39,865
Did you kill her?

12
00:00:44,957 --> 00:00:48,265
[male #1]
'Mercy's father would like
to give a brief statement.'

13
00:00:48,352 --> 00:00:51,007
I just want to take a moment
and thank everyone

14
00:00:51,094 --> 00:00:53,879
in law enforcement
and all the volunteers

15
00:00:53,966 --> 00:00:56,360
who helped us in the search
for our beloved daughter.

16
00:00:58,797 --> 00:01:00,451
'The way that this
entire community'

17
00:01:00,538 --> 00:01:04,760
has come together
to support me and Juniper

18
00:01:04,847 --> 00:01:08,111
in this terrible time
has been a great comfort to us.

19
00:01:11,158 --> 00:01:14,813
'And now I would just
like to ask you that..'

20
00:01:14,900 --> 00:01:18,513
'..you give us some time,
space and privacy'

21
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:20,036
'to grieve for our daughter.'

22
00:01:20,123 --> 00:01:21,516
'Thank you.'

23
00:01:25,259 --> 00:01:28,131
[indistinct radio chatter]

24
00:01:50,588 --> 00:01:52,460
[rustling]

25
00:02:25,275 --> 00:02:28,148
[teakettle whistling]

26
00:02:30,237 --> 00:02:32,152
[whistling stops]

27
00:02:39,246 --> 00:02:41,987
Hello, Mrs. Tolliver.

28
00:02:42,074 --> 00:02:43,728
Who are you?

29
00:02:43,815 --> 00:02:46,166
My name is Patrick Jane.

30
00:02:46,253 --> 00:02:48,994
I'm here to help you.

31
00:02:49,081 --> 00:02:50,996
Would you like a cup of tea?

32
00:02:53,347 --> 00:02:55,914
Yes, I would, thank you.

33
00:02:58,917 --> 00:03:00,310
You must be tired.

34
00:03:01,746 --> 00:03:03,357
Why don't you sit down?

35
00:03:05,620 --> 00:03:06,664
It's nice and quiet
in here, isn't it?

36
00:03:08,405 --> 00:03:10,625
Quiet, soothing, calm.

37
00:03:13,671 --> 00:03:14,629
Calm.

38
00:03:14,716 --> 00:03:15,847
[sighs]

39
00:03:22,376 --> 00:03:24,334
I've been watching you
and your husband

40
00:03:24,421 --> 00:03:26,118
and I want you to know
that I understand

41
00:03:26,206 --> 00:03:27,729
what you're feeling
right now.

42
00:03:30,906 --> 00:03:32,429
You have no idea.

43
00:03:34,866 --> 00:03:36,564
Believe me.

44
00:03:36,651 --> 00:03:37,913
I do.

45
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:40,263
I know.

46
00:03:40,350 --> 00:03:41,569
I know,
and I wanna help you.

47
00:03:41,656 --> 00:03:43,875
You can't help me.

48
00:03:43,962 --> 00:03:46,138
You..
What do you know?

49
00:03:46,226 --> 00:03:48,228
[chuckles]
All sorts of things.

50
00:03:50,142 --> 00:03:52,928
You really only pretend
to like skiing, right?

51
00:03:53,015 --> 00:03:54,277
Yes, but--

52
00:03:54,364 --> 00:03:55,844
You're pleased
that your best friend

53
00:03:55,931 --> 00:03:58,629
recently gained some weight.
About 10 pounds.

54
00:03:58,716 --> 00:03:59,891
You wish you'd been
more adventurous

55
00:03:59,978 --> 00:04:01,328
when you were younger.

56
00:04:01,415 --> 00:04:03,330
You love India,
but you've never been there.

57
00:04:03,417 --> 00:04:06,376
You have trouble sleeping.
Your favorite color..

58
00:04:08,465 --> 00:04:10,859
...is blue.

59
00:04:10,946 --> 00:04:14,819
I don't understand.
You're..

60
00:04:14,906 --> 00:04:15,907
You're psychic?

61
00:04:15,994 --> 00:04:17,953
[chuckles]
No.

62
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:20,303
Just paying attention.

63
00:04:20,390 --> 00:04:23,741
I used to make a good living
pretending to be a psychic.

64
00:04:25,308 --> 00:04:28,355
I tell you this because
I want you to understand

65
00:04:28,442 --> 00:04:30,922
there's no point
hiding things from me.

66
00:04:33,360 --> 00:04:35,579
Hiding...what?

67
00:04:35,666 --> 00:04:39,409
You know what I see
when I look at your husband?

68
00:04:39,496 --> 00:04:42,847
I see a warm, loving,
generous man.

69
00:04:42,934 --> 00:04:44,545
A little vain, maybe.

70
00:04:44,632 --> 00:04:46,590
Selfish, controlling..

71
00:04:46,677 --> 00:04:48,200
...but a decent man.

72
00:04:48,288 --> 00:04:49,289
Yes.

73
00:04:52,988 --> 00:04:55,425
So why do you suspect him
of murdering your daughter?

74
00:04:55,512 --> 00:04:58,385
[teacup rattling]

75
00:04:59,864 --> 00:05:01,126
I don't.

76
00:05:03,346 --> 00:05:05,566
- The McCluskey boy did it.
- Yes.

77
00:05:05,653 --> 00:05:08,046
That's what the police say.

78
00:05:08,133 --> 00:05:11,702
But you think
they're wrong. Why?

79
00:05:11,789 --> 00:05:13,965
I don't know.
I-I-I don't know.

80
00:05:14,052 --> 00:05:15,793
I..

81
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:17,839
Tell me.

82
00:05:17,926 --> 00:05:19,580
Last year,

83
00:05:19,667 --> 00:05:23,061
they-they have been
so strange with each other.

84
00:05:23,148 --> 00:05:25,542
And neither one would admit
that anything was wrong

85
00:05:25,629 --> 00:05:29,198
and I think that..

86
00:05:29,285 --> 00:05:31,026
I think that she tried
to tell me once

87
00:05:31,113 --> 00:05:33,333
and I didn't..
I...

88
00:05:35,726 --> 00:05:37,511
God.

89
00:05:37,598 --> 00:05:39,251
Oh, God.

90
00:05:39,339 --> 00:05:40,992
Did you ask him
if he killed her?

91
00:05:41,079 --> 00:05:42,777
[sniffles]

92
00:05:42,864 --> 00:05:44,387
What would he say?

93
00:05:44,474 --> 00:05:47,085
Most wives can tell
when their husbands are lying.

94
00:05:49,479 --> 00:05:53,570
Yes. Yes. I..

95
00:05:53,657 --> 00:05:56,617
I don't want tea. I..
The McCluskey boy did it. I..

96
00:05:56,704 --> 00:05:57,792
Maybe.

97
00:05:59,663 --> 00:06:03,058
[whispers]
Oh.

98
00:06:03,145 --> 00:06:06,148
You think he did it, too?

99
00:06:06,235 --> 00:06:09,456
I trust a mother's instinct.

100
00:06:09,543 --> 00:06:10,761
[door opens]

101
00:06:10,848 --> 00:06:13,155
June?

102
00:06:13,242 --> 00:06:14,199
[sighs]

103
00:06:14,286 --> 00:06:16,593
'There you are.'

104
00:06:16,680 --> 00:06:19,379
Hi. Who are you?

105
00:06:19,466 --> 00:06:21,946
I'm the police.
Did you kill your daughter?

106
00:06:26,124 --> 00:06:27,343
[scoffs]

107
00:06:27,430 --> 00:06:28,910
How dare you?

108
00:06:28,997 --> 00:06:30,651
I asked you
a simple question, sir.

109
00:06:30,738 --> 00:06:33,567
Did you kill your daughter?

110
00:06:33,654 --> 00:06:34,959
- No.
- Oh!

111
00:06:35,046 --> 00:06:37,527
I did not kill my daughter!

112
00:06:37,614 --> 00:06:40,487
Now you get the hell
out of my house!

113
00:06:41,749 --> 00:06:43,490
June?

114
00:06:43,577 --> 00:06:45,883
June, what's the matter
with you?

115
00:06:48,059 --> 00:06:49,626
I'm gonna have your badge.

116
00:06:49,713 --> 00:06:52,673
An innocent man
would have punched me by now.

117
00:06:52,760 --> 00:06:54,849
I am gonna make life
miserable for you.

118
00:06:54,936 --> 00:06:57,504
You come in here,
you accost my wife

119
00:06:57,591 --> 00:06:58,940
you cause trouble on..

120
00:06:59,027 --> 00:07:00,376
[cocks pistol]

121
00:07:00,463 --> 00:07:04,162
June.
June, honey, please.

122
00:07:04,249 --> 00:07:05,642
[gunshots fired]

123
00:07:05,729 --> 00:07:07,557
[officers shouting
indistinctly]

124
00:07:07,644 --> 00:07:09,690
[male #2]
'Move! Move! Hey!'

125
00:07:14,869 --> 00:07:16,479
Honestly, it-it's not
as bad as it looks.

126
00:07:18,742 --> 00:07:20,352
[indistinct radio chatter]

127
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:21,832
Mrs. Tolliver?

128
00:07:21,919 --> 00:07:24,661
Mrs. Tolliver!
Please wait.

129
00:07:24,748 --> 00:07:26,533
[male #2]
Front room's clear!

130
00:07:49,947 --> 00:07:52,341
Then the son of a bitch
eagles 17.

131
00:07:52,428 --> 00:07:54,909
Are you kiddin' me?
On that course?

132
00:07:54,996 --> 00:07:56,998
A damn eagle?

133
00:07:57,085 --> 00:07:58,826
That course never
suited you, Price.

134
00:07:58,913 --> 00:08:02,003
We'll do better in Orlando.
We have a nice spot on the draw.

135
00:08:02,090 --> 00:08:03,570
Well, I'll tell you what.

136
00:08:03,657 --> 00:08:06,181
Davis Love III
can kiss my butt.

137
00:08:17,671 --> 00:08:19,411
[male #3]
Alison?

138
00:08:19,499 --> 00:08:21,109
Alison!

139
00:08:29,160 --> 00:08:32,033
[indistinct chatter]

140
00:08:33,904 --> 00:08:35,993
[woman over PA]
'Flight 233 from Sacramento'

141
00:08:36,080 --> 00:08:39,127
'you may claim your baggage
from carousel 2.'

142
00:08:39,214 --> 00:08:41,608
'Flight 233 from Sacramento...'

143
00:08:41,695 --> 00:08:43,610
Uh, sorry.

144
00:08:43,697 --> 00:08:46,526
You checked luggage?
What are you, on vacation?

145
00:08:46,613 --> 00:08:48,223
No, ma'am.
Won't do it again.

146
00:08:48,310 --> 00:08:50,225
When your trousseau arrives,
pick up the second rental

147
00:08:50,312 --> 00:08:52,227
and go direct
to the sheriff's department

148
00:08:52,314 --> 00:08:55,186
hustle us up a couple of rooms,
furniture and phone lines.

149
00:08:55,273 --> 00:08:56,231
Yes. Ma'am.

150
00:08:56,318 --> 00:08:58,102
Come on. Let's go.

151
00:08:58,189 --> 00:08:59,800
[Lisbon sighs]

152
00:09:07,634 --> 00:09:10,854
Morning, everybody.
How was your flight?

153
00:09:10,941 --> 00:09:13,727
Go away.
You're on suspension.

154
00:09:13,814 --> 00:09:14,902
Thank you.

155
00:09:16,338 --> 00:09:18,296
Mandated leave.
Ends next week.

156
00:09:18,383 --> 00:09:19,863
So come back next week.

157
00:09:19,950 --> 00:09:21,212
Hot enough for you?

158
00:09:21,299 --> 00:09:23,171
Which one of you jackasses
told him?

159
00:09:23,258 --> 00:09:25,216
- It was you, wasn't it, Cho?
- Yes, it was.

160
00:09:25,303 --> 00:09:27,218
Of course he called me.
It's Red John.

161
00:09:27,305 --> 00:09:30,091
You can't keep me out of this.
Why would you want to?

162
00:09:30,178 --> 00:09:32,006
You got a man killed.
There's consequences.

163
00:09:32,093 --> 00:09:33,529
Oh, a man
that murdered his daughter

164
00:09:33,616 --> 00:09:35,313
'cause she wouldn't have sex
with him anymore?

165
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:37,489
You didn't know that.
You didnotknow that.

166
00:09:37,577 --> 00:09:38,969
If she hadn't had left
a diary--

167
00:09:39,056 --> 00:09:41,711
But she did, though.
Be reasonable. This is my case.

168
00:09:41,798 --> 00:09:44,148
- Your case?
- Red John's mine.

169
00:09:44,235 --> 00:09:46,194
Red john
doesn't belong to anyone.

170
00:09:46,281 --> 00:09:49,284
[sighs]

171
00:09:49,371 --> 00:09:50,981
He belongs to me.

172
00:09:51,068 --> 00:09:53,636
It's not my call.
Rules are rules.

173
00:09:53,723 --> 00:09:56,291
Come back next week.

174
00:09:56,378 --> 00:09:58,598
Don't let this man past.

175
00:10:01,078 --> 00:10:03,646
[cell phone rings]

176
00:10:03,733 --> 00:10:05,169
[ring]

177
00:10:05,256 --> 00:10:06,257
[beep]

178
00:10:06,344 --> 00:10:07,737
Boss?

179
00:10:07,824 --> 00:10:09,260
We have Gregory Tannen

180
00:10:09,347 --> 00:10:12,220
Caucasian, male,
43, single.

181
00:10:12,307 --> 00:10:14,091
'We haven't opened him up yet,
but burn marks..'

182
00:10:14,178 --> 00:10:17,834
Sorry I went over your head.
I'll redeem myself, I promise.

183
00:10:17,921 --> 00:10:19,967
You want redemption?
Be silent.

184
00:10:20,054 --> 00:10:21,751
- Okay. I can learn to do that.
- Shh!

185
00:10:24,667 --> 00:10:25,842
Sorry.

186
00:10:27,714 --> 00:10:30,412
The burn marks here
indicate that the victim

187
00:10:30,499 --> 00:10:32,327
'was subdued with a stun gun'

188
00:10:32,414 --> 00:10:34,634
'standard civilian model
by the look of it.'

189
00:10:34,721 --> 00:10:35,939
Death appears to be caused

190
00:10:36,026 --> 00:10:37,767
by several blows
to the back of the skull

191
00:10:37,854 --> 00:10:40,944
'consistent with a bloodied
golf club found at the scene.'

192
00:10:41,031 --> 00:10:46,167
'Female is Alison Randolph
27, married, no children.'

193
00:10:46,254 --> 00:10:48,125
'They were found
at her listed residence.'

194
00:10:48,212 --> 00:10:50,345
'TOD looks to be
early Saturday evening.'

195
00:10:50,432 --> 00:10:52,303
'On Alison, we have
the same stun gun marks'

196
00:10:52,390 --> 00:10:55,393
'followed by binding with
tight black plastic ligatures'

197
00:10:55,480 --> 00:10:57,874
frenzied cutting and stabbing
assault of the torso

198
00:10:57,961 --> 00:10:59,528
and subsequent abuse
of the viscera.

199
00:10:59,615 --> 00:11:01,573
- Textbook Red John.
- Who found the bodies?

200
00:11:01,661 --> 00:11:03,750
This one's husband, coming home
from the airport Sunday morning

201
00:11:03,837 --> 00:11:05,708
'with his brother.
He's a pro golfer.'

202
00:11:05,795 --> 00:11:07,928
- Oh, yeah?
- Price Randolph.

203
00:11:08,015 --> 00:11:09,973
What's her deal with him?
Do we know?

204
00:11:10,060 --> 00:11:11,758
Uh, he's on file
as one of her physicians.

205
00:11:11,845 --> 00:11:13,498
- Making a house call?
- Lovers?

206
00:11:13,585 --> 00:11:15,675
No, this one's gay.

207
00:11:17,938 --> 00:11:20,854
Dr. Wagner might know
what their relationship was.

208
00:11:20,941 --> 00:11:23,683
He's here
to make the formal I.D.?

209
00:11:23,770 --> 00:11:25,423
Okay.

210
00:11:25,510 --> 00:11:27,991
Dr. Wagner.

211
00:11:28,078 --> 00:11:30,211
Hi.

212
00:11:30,298 --> 00:11:31,734
I'm Agent Teresa Lisbon

213
00:11:31,821 --> 00:11:33,954
California bureau
of investigation.

214
00:11:34,041 --> 00:11:35,651
What's your connection
to the victims?

215
00:11:35,738 --> 00:11:37,087
I work with Gregory.

216
00:11:37,174 --> 00:11:39,655
Dr. Tannen and-and
the Randolph family

217
00:11:39,742 --> 00:11:41,744
are longtime clients
of our practice.

218
00:11:41,831 --> 00:11:43,790
Are house calls the norm
at your practice?

219
00:11:43,877 --> 00:11:46,880
No. Gregory and Alison
were close friends.

220
00:11:46,967 --> 00:11:49,447
- Lovers?
- No. He was gay.

221
00:11:49,534 --> 00:11:52,929
No, they were just...
friends.

222
00:11:53,016 --> 00:11:54,931
What in God's name
happened to them?

223
00:11:55,018 --> 00:11:56,454
Looks like Red John.

224
00:11:57,934 --> 00:11:59,501
Who's Red John?

225
00:11:59,588 --> 00:12:01,677
We don't know who did this.

226
00:12:01,764 --> 00:12:04,767
We'll be in touch probably.
Thank you.

227
00:12:11,078 --> 00:12:13,471
- 'Set up right here?'
- 'Yeah, that's good.'

228
00:12:13,558 --> 00:12:15,909
Red John enters here.

229
00:12:15,996 --> 00:12:17,867
Excuse me. Sorry.

230
00:12:17,954 --> 00:12:20,261
He comes around here.

231
00:12:20,348 --> 00:12:22,829
'He waits for her..'

232
00:12:22,916 --> 00:12:24,874
'...expecting her
to come in alone.'

233
00:12:24,961 --> 00:12:27,659
Only thing, her friend Tannen
Chose the wrong night

234
00:12:27,747 --> 00:12:30,010
to come over for a Richard Gere
and ice cream orgy.

235
00:12:31,881 --> 00:12:35,755
So Red John zaps 'em both
with his trusty stun gun

236
00:12:35,842 --> 00:12:36,799
and...

237
00:12:36,886 --> 00:12:38,496
...excuse me.

238
00:12:38,583 --> 00:12:41,717
Grabs a 5-iron
from the bag here and..

239
00:12:41,804 --> 00:12:43,414
Bam!

240
00:12:46,069 --> 00:12:47,679
Crushes Tannen's skull.

241
00:12:47,767 --> 00:12:49,290
'Then he takes his sweet time'

242
00:12:49,377 --> 00:12:52,119
'dealing with Alison
how he likes.'

243
00:12:52,206 --> 00:12:55,775
She's a nice big girl,
so unless he's pretty strong

244
00:12:55,862 --> 00:12:57,994
'I'm guessing that he grabbed
her by the arms and...'

245
00:13:37,251 --> 00:13:39,383
He says he's sorry
for all the pain

246
00:13:39,470 --> 00:13:41,472
he's caused you
and your mother.

247
00:13:43,083 --> 00:13:44,432
Deeply sorry.

248
00:13:44,519 --> 00:13:45,737
[woman sniffles]

249
00:13:45,825 --> 00:13:48,523
He asks you to forgive him.

250
00:13:48,610 --> 00:13:50,568
Can you do that, Jenny?

251
00:13:50,655 --> 00:13:52,353
[crying]
Mm-hmm.

252
00:13:52,440 --> 00:13:54,964
- He needs to hear it.
- I forgive you, daddy.

253
00:13:55,051 --> 00:13:56,357
- Oh, yes.
- Daddy, I forgive you.

254
00:13:56,444 --> 00:13:57,837
[cries]

255
00:13:57,924 --> 00:13:59,229
He's smiling now.

256
00:13:59,316 --> 00:14:00,491
[laughs]

257
00:14:00,578 --> 00:14:01,753
They're tears of joy.

258
00:14:01,841 --> 00:14:03,886
[cries]

259
00:14:03,973 --> 00:14:06,236
He says, "God bless you
and keep you."

260
00:14:06,323 --> 00:14:07,716
[continues crying]

261
00:14:12,025 --> 00:14:13,765
He's gone.

262
00:14:25,081 --> 00:14:27,605
Amazing. Amazing. Amazing.

263
00:14:27,692 --> 00:14:29,346
She's...amazed.

264
00:14:29,433 --> 00:14:31,566
[laughter]

265
00:14:31,653 --> 00:14:33,655
- Patrick..
- One second.

266
00:14:33,742 --> 00:14:35,222
- Give him some time.
- Ab-absolu..

267
00:14:35,309 --> 00:14:36,701
Come on back to us.

268
00:14:36,788 --> 00:14:39,226
- I'm back. Thank you.
- He's back.

269
00:14:39,313 --> 00:14:42,925
So, Patrick, I understand
that you're also

270
00:14:43,012 --> 00:14:46,668
sort of a paranormal
detective. Is that right?

271
00:14:46,755 --> 00:14:48,888
I try to help the police
when I can.

272
00:14:48,975 --> 00:14:51,020
And-and you're
helping them hunt

273
00:14:51,107 --> 00:14:53,327
this scary serial killer.

274
00:14:53,414 --> 00:14:54,371
What's his name?

275
00:14:54,458 --> 00:14:55,938
- Red--
- Red john?

276
00:14:56,025 --> 00:15:00,160
- There she blows..
- Classic Red John smiley face.

277
00:15:00,247 --> 00:15:02,727
Drawn in the victims' blood

278
00:15:02,814 --> 00:15:06,775
clockwise with three fingers
of his right hand

279
00:15:06,862 --> 00:15:09,343
wearing a rubber
kitchen glove.

280
00:15:09,430 --> 00:15:12,041
I'm stoked to finally
see one in the flesh.

281
00:15:12,128 --> 00:15:13,477
This isn't Red John.

282
00:15:14,783 --> 00:15:16,654
Right.

283
00:15:16,741 --> 00:15:19,657
Red john thinks of himself
as a showman, an artist.

284
00:15:19,744 --> 00:15:21,485
'He has a strong sense
of theater.'

285
00:15:21,572 --> 00:15:23,226
In all the previous killings,
he made sure

286
00:15:23,313 --> 00:15:27,665
that the first thing that anyone
sees is the face on the wall.

287
00:15:27,752 --> 00:15:30,146
'You see the face first,
and you know..'

288
00:15:30,233 --> 00:15:32,714
'...you know what's happened,
and you feel dread.'

289
00:15:32,801 --> 00:15:35,586
Then and only then do you see
the body of the victim.

290
00:15:35,673 --> 00:15:37,240
'Always in that order.'

291
00:15:37,327 --> 00:15:38,938
Here it's the opposite.

292
00:15:39,025 --> 00:15:41,636
The first thing you see
is the body

293
00:15:41,723 --> 00:15:45,118
and you have to look around
to see the face on the wall.

294
00:15:45,205 --> 00:15:47,337
Doesn't play nearly
as well, does it?

295
00:15:47,424 --> 00:15:49,774
Depends on your taste,
I suppose.

296
00:15:49,861 --> 00:15:51,776
No, come on. The killer
could have painted

297
00:15:51,863 --> 00:15:53,343
on the correct wall here,

298
00:15:53,430 --> 00:15:55,041
but he didn't
because he didn't know better

299
00:15:55,128 --> 00:15:57,086
because he isn't Red John.

300
00:15:57,173 --> 00:16:01,134
Wow. It's interesting.

301
00:16:01,221 --> 00:16:02,787
[sighs deeply]

302
00:16:02,874 --> 00:16:05,399
You know what
your problem is, my friend?

303
00:16:05,486 --> 00:16:08,184
You enjoy your work a little
too much. You're a ghoul.

304
00:16:10,056 --> 00:16:11,666
If you don't get horny
reading "Fangoria"

305
00:16:11,753 --> 00:16:12,928
I'm Britney Spears.

306
00:16:13,015 --> 00:16:14,582
I-I resent that.

307
00:16:14,669 --> 00:16:16,540
This is you trying
to redeem yourself, is it?

308
00:16:16,627 --> 00:16:19,021
I'm sorry.

309
00:16:19,108 --> 00:16:21,284
He irks me.

310
00:16:21,371 --> 00:16:22,503
He's irksome.

311
00:16:24,505 --> 00:16:25,985
You don't need me here.

312
00:16:41,609 --> 00:16:44,525
So, yeah, this one
doesn't fit the pattern.

313
00:16:44,612 --> 00:16:46,179
So Jane was right.
We have a copycat.

314
00:16:46,266 --> 00:16:48,485
Or we have Red John
trying new things

315
00:16:48,572 --> 00:16:50,270
'or we have Red John
making a mistake.'

316
00:16:50,357 --> 00:16:53,969
We don't know. We'll work
the evidence until we do know.

317
00:16:54,056 --> 00:16:56,580
- Go talk to the husband.
- Will do, boss.

318
00:17:01,542 --> 00:17:03,152
What are you waitin' for?

319
00:17:20,865 --> 00:17:22,650
[dialing]

320
00:17:24,782 --> 00:17:27,524
Hey. So you might be right
about this case.

321
00:17:27,611 --> 00:17:29,483
Might be.
Thanks for the insight.

322
00:17:31,093 --> 00:17:33,052
No. Did I say that?

323
00:17:33,139 --> 00:17:36,707
I'm acknowledging the fact that
you might be right, that's all.

324
00:17:36,794 --> 00:17:38,144
I mean, if you wanted
to come back

325
00:17:38,231 --> 00:17:39,580
I couldn't stop you.

326
00:17:41,538 --> 00:17:44,150
Yeah, fine.
I'm asking you to come back.

327
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:48,328
Because.

328
00:17:48,415 --> 00:17:50,286
Because you're useful
to the team.

329
00:17:52,158 --> 00:17:54,551
No. No, I won't say "please."
Go screw yourself.

330
00:17:54,638 --> 00:17:55,683
[beep]

331
00:17:55,770 --> 00:17:57,032
Jackass.

332
00:18:06,911 --> 00:18:08,391
[Jane]
'Good morning.'

333
00:18:08,478 --> 00:18:09,784
Can I help you?

334
00:18:11,525 --> 00:18:13,353
You must be Van Pelt.

335
00:18:13,440 --> 00:18:15,006
Pleasure. Patrick Jane.

336
00:18:15,094 --> 00:18:16,834
Oh, hi. Good to meet you.

337
00:18:16,921 --> 00:18:18,445
Agent Cho said
you had left town.

338
00:18:18,532 --> 00:18:21,100
No. Nowhere to go.

339
00:18:21,187 --> 00:18:23,058
Okay. Um..

340
00:18:23,145 --> 00:18:26,017
Do you want that desk
over there or this one?

341
00:18:26,105 --> 00:18:27,802
I mean,
that one gets more light.

342
00:18:27,889 --> 00:18:29,978
That one.
More light by all means.

343
00:18:30,065 --> 00:18:32,372
[chuckles]

344
00:18:32,459 --> 00:18:34,983
Very pleasant addition
to the serious crimes family.

345
00:18:35,070 --> 00:18:37,464
Oh. Hi.
When did you get here?

346
00:18:37,551 --> 00:18:41,032
Oh!Stop. I give up. Ooh!

347
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:43,948
'Stop. Please, stop.
Turn off the camera.'

348
00:18:44,035 --> 00:18:45,254
'Come on, come on, come on.'

349
00:18:45,341 --> 00:18:47,343
'Okay, we're done, we're done.'

350
00:18:47,430 --> 00:18:49,650
'You are just awful!'

351
00:18:49,737 --> 00:18:51,130
Okay.
Go, go, go.

352
00:18:51,217 --> 00:18:53,958
'Stop, please. Stop!'

353
00:18:54,045 --> 00:18:55,612
[click]

354
00:18:58,441 --> 00:19:00,617
I lost a beautiful,
precious angel.

355
00:19:03,229 --> 00:19:04,752
Yes, sir.

356
00:19:04,839 --> 00:19:06,449
Good-looking woman.

357
00:19:08,234 --> 00:19:09,800
[clears throat]

358
00:19:09,887 --> 00:19:11,846
I'm jumping right in
if you don't mind, Price.

359
00:19:11,933 --> 00:19:14,153
'You missed the tournament
cut on Friday, yes?'

360
00:19:14,240 --> 00:19:15,850
'But you didn't come home
until Sunday.'

361
00:19:15,937 --> 00:19:17,939
What did you do with the rest
of your time in Fresno?

362
00:19:18,026 --> 00:19:20,289
I get this. You-you guys can't
catch the real killer

363
00:19:20,376 --> 00:19:22,291
so you wanna
lay this one on me?

364
00:19:22,378 --> 00:19:24,424
No, sir. If we have that
confirmation of where you were

365
00:19:24,511 --> 00:19:26,861
it lets us exclude you
from the investigation.

366
00:19:36,436 --> 00:19:39,700
[chuckles]
I was with a massage therapist.

367
00:19:39,787 --> 00:19:41,963
Name?

368
00:19:42,050 --> 00:19:46,750
Uh...it had "lady"
in there somewhere.

369
00:19:46,837 --> 00:19:48,796
It'll be
on his credit card bill.

370
00:19:48,883 --> 00:19:50,406
'There you go.'

371
00:19:50,493 --> 00:19:51,799
Pleasure meeting you boys.

372
00:19:55,194 --> 00:19:58,197
[Wagner]
'We're a full-service
private practice.'

373
00:19:58,284 --> 00:20:00,721
'We deliver primary care'

374
00:20:00,808 --> 00:20:02,853
'uh, cosmetic surgery'

375
00:20:02,940 --> 00:20:05,769
psychotherapy, sports medicine..
You name it.

376
00:20:05,856 --> 00:20:07,423
What's the African connection?

377
00:20:07,510 --> 00:20:09,730
It's what
this place is all about.

378
00:20:09,817 --> 00:20:12,080
Half our profits
go to build and staff

379
00:20:12,167 --> 00:20:15,779
basic health clinics
in poor African communities.

380
00:20:15,866 --> 00:20:17,346
Ah, here we are.

381
00:20:17,433 --> 00:20:19,609
[sighs]

382
00:20:19,696 --> 00:20:22,003
'It's a thin file.'

383
00:20:22,090 --> 00:20:24,701
'Alison was
a healthy young woman.'

384
00:20:24,788 --> 00:20:26,703
Psychiatric history?

385
00:20:26,790 --> 00:20:28,488
She didn't have one.

386
00:20:28,575 --> 00:20:30,490
[Lisbon]
'STDS? Abortions?'

387
00:20:30,577 --> 00:20:32,405
'Unexplained injuries?'

388
00:20:32,492 --> 00:20:35,103
[Wagner]
'No. Except for some
routine checkups with me'

389
00:20:35,190 --> 00:20:37,497
'it's all Dr. Tannen.
All aesthetic work.'

390
00:20:37,584 --> 00:20:39,281
Did Tannen keep a diary?

391
00:20:39,368 --> 00:20:43,024
Our last case was solved
because the victim kept a diary.

392
00:20:43,111 --> 00:20:45,200
Diary? I don't think so.

393
00:20:45,287 --> 00:20:47,158
Getting back
to Alison Randolph...

394
00:20:47,246 --> 00:20:50,292
'how was her marriage,
do you think?'

395
00:20:50,379 --> 00:20:52,338
Happy? Unhappy?

396
00:20:52,425 --> 00:20:54,209
About six months ago

397
00:20:54,296 --> 00:20:57,734
Dr. Tannen asked my advice.

398
00:20:57,821 --> 00:20:59,214
'Alison had asked him
to get her'

399
00:20:59,301 --> 00:21:01,085
a year's supply
of birth control pills

400
00:21:01,172 --> 00:21:04,524
off the books, which is
strictly against AMA Code.

401
00:21:04,611 --> 00:21:07,918
'I said sure, do it.'

402
00:21:08,005 --> 00:21:12,662
'I mean, better us
than some Tijuana drugstore.

403
00:21:12,749 --> 00:21:14,838
Why the secrecy?

404
00:21:14,925 --> 00:21:18,755
Price Randolph had
a vasectomy, April of '02.

405
00:21:18,842 --> 00:21:20,061
[chuckles]

406
00:21:20,148 --> 00:21:22,193
If there's anything else
I can do...

407
00:21:22,281 --> 00:21:23,586
I appreciate that.

408
00:21:25,588 --> 00:21:27,677
Actually, there is. Uh..

409
00:21:27,764 --> 00:21:30,114
I'm out of sleeping pills.

410
00:21:30,201 --> 00:21:32,595
Can you fix me up?
Anything strong will do.

411
00:21:32,682 --> 00:21:34,989
Sure. Uh, come in
for a consultation.

412
00:21:35,076 --> 00:21:36,556
We'll squeeze you in
this afternoon.

413
00:21:36,643 --> 00:21:39,210
Oh, no. I-I was hoping
to get something now.

414
00:21:39,298 --> 00:21:41,169
Trying to avoid the chitchat.

415
00:21:41,256 --> 00:21:42,953
I'm sorry.

416
00:21:43,040 --> 00:21:45,347
I wouldn't feel
comfortable prescribing

417
00:21:45,434 --> 00:21:47,871
without some sort
of "chitchat."

418
00:21:47,958 --> 00:21:50,744
I understand.
Uh, no problem.

419
00:21:50,831 --> 00:21:52,267
I'll call you..

420
00:21:52,354 --> 00:21:53,660
...maybe.

421
00:21:56,184 --> 00:21:57,794
[Cho]
'I like the husband for it.'

422
00:21:57,881 --> 00:21:59,492
'He hires some hooker he knows
to create an alibi'

423
00:21:59,579 --> 00:22:02,016
flies home, fillets the spouse,
flies back again.

424
00:22:02,103 --> 00:22:05,367
The classic elaborate and clever
but ultimately stupid plan.

425
00:22:05,454 --> 00:22:07,369
Have you looked at
his PGA tournament record?

426
00:22:07,456 --> 00:22:09,415
It's not bad.
6 mil career earnings.

427
00:22:09,502 --> 00:22:11,721
Mm-hmm, for coming in
second and third.

428
00:22:11,808 --> 00:22:14,245
'You put him on the 18th tee
with a big one on the line'

429
00:22:14,333 --> 00:22:17,814
like night follows day,
he'll shank it. He's a Choker.

430
00:22:17,901 --> 00:22:19,947
He doesn't have the nerve
to kill his wife. Didn't do it.

431
00:22:20,034 --> 00:22:21,340
Mm.

432
00:22:21,427 --> 00:22:23,342
Are you suggesting
we drop a prime suspect

433
00:22:23,429 --> 00:22:24,995
'because he's never
won a major?'

434
00:22:25,082 --> 00:22:29,435
'Oh, no, no, no. I'm just
making idle conversation.'

435
00:22:29,522 --> 00:22:31,828
How'd you do that?

436
00:22:31,915 --> 00:22:33,656
Telekinesis.

437
00:22:33,743 --> 00:22:35,832
He blew on it.

438
00:22:37,530 --> 00:22:39,009
That is another way
to do it.

439
00:22:40,707 --> 00:22:42,622
Mr. Jane..

440
00:22:42,709 --> 00:22:45,451
...I have a question regarding
your previous career path.

441
00:22:45,538 --> 00:22:47,061
Fire away.

442
00:22:47,148 --> 00:22:50,194
When you met with other
psychics, real psychics

443
00:22:50,281 --> 00:22:52,849
could they tell
you were just pretending?

444
00:22:52,936 --> 00:22:54,982
There's no such thing
as real psychics.

445
00:22:55,069 --> 00:22:58,028
I beg to differ.
My cousin Yolanda is a psychic.

446
00:22:58,115 --> 00:23:00,683
Your cousin is deluded
or dishonest, or both.

447
00:23:00,770 --> 00:23:02,206
Hey. Steady.

448
00:23:02,293 --> 00:23:04,557
No, no, he's entitled
to his opinion.

449
00:23:04,644 --> 00:23:06,733
He's wrong, though.
She has power.

450
00:23:06,820 --> 00:23:08,169
Thank you.

451
00:23:08,256 --> 00:23:09,997
She can communicate
with the other side.

452
00:23:10,084 --> 00:23:11,520
I've seen her do it myself.

453
00:23:11,607 --> 00:23:13,479
She let you speak
with someone that's gone.

454
00:23:13,566 --> 00:23:15,350
Yes.

455
00:23:15,437 --> 00:23:17,744
Someone that you love
and still miss very much.

456
00:23:17,831 --> 00:23:19,267
Yes.

457
00:23:19,354 --> 00:23:22,052
You wanted her power
to be real, so it was.

458
00:23:22,139 --> 00:23:23,924
No.

459
00:23:24,011 --> 00:23:26,709
You're so sure you're right.
Science don't know everything.

460
00:23:26,796 --> 00:23:28,972
500 years ago, radio would've
seemed like magic.

461
00:23:29,059 --> 00:23:30,060
Exactly.

462
00:23:30,147 --> 00:23:31,845
500 years in the future,

463
00:23:31,932 --> 00:23:33,368
it could be totally normal to
communicate with the other side.

464
00:23:33,455 --> 00:23:37,807
- The "other side."
- Mm-hmm.

465
00:23:37,894 --> 00:23:40,506
Your father's
a football coach, yeah?

466
00:23:40,593 --> 00:23:42,508
How'd you know that?

467
00:23:42,595 --> 00:23:44,553
It's obvious
from your whole demeanor.

468
00:23:44,640 --> 00:23:48,731
My point is, didn't dad always
say life is like football?

469
00:23:48,818 --> 00:23:51,473
When that final whistle blows,
the game is over.

470
00:23:51,560 --> 00:23:53,954
Done. There is no more.

471
00:23:54,041 --> 00:23:57,087
There is no "other side."
this is it..

472
00:23:57,174 --> 00:23:59,568
Lobster and bread rolls
and nautical kitsch.

473
00:23:59,655 --> 00:24:02,397
And then...nothingness.

474
00:24:02,484 --> 00:24:04,443
You poor, sad man.

475
00:24:04,530 --> 00:24:06,836
The kingdom of God
is a real place.

476
00:24:06,923 --> 00:24:09,404
Okay, later tonight,

477
00:24:09,491 --> 00:24:12,363
when Rigsby asks you to
come back to his hotel room..

478
00:24:12,451 --> 00:24:14,540
[choking and coughing]

479
00:24:16,498 --> 00:24:18,935
- ...say yes.
- Excuse me?

480
00:24:19,022 --> 00:24:22,112
I know. You were planning on
refusing him very curtly.

481
00:24:22,199 --> 00:24:24,114
First week on the job,
you wanna set a tone.

482
00:24:24,201 --> 00:24:26,116
No monkey business.
But why not?

483
00:24:26,203 --> 00:24:28,118
Rigsby is an excellent lover,
I'm sure.

484
00:24:28,205 --> 00:24:29,250
[sighs]

485
00:24:29,337 --> 00:24:32,296
Tough but fair. Right?

486
00:24:32,383 --> 00:24:33,733
Right.

487
00:24:39,347 --> 00:24:42,481
The kingdom of God
is a real place, Mr. Jane

488
00:24:42,568 --> 00:24:45,396
and you have
an immortal soul.

489
00:24:45,484 --> 00:24:47,703
Oh, I do so hope
you're wrong.

490
00:24:51,751 --> 00:24:54,318
[elevator bell chimes]

491
00:24:54,405 --> 00:24:55,581
- Goodnight.
- Goodnight.

492
00:24:55,668 --> 00:24:56,930
Later, dude.

493
00:25:03,197 --> 00:25:04,633
[elevator bell dings]

494
00:25:04,720 --> 00:25:06,243
This is... me.

495
00:25:06,330 --> 00:25:07,810
[elevator bell chimes]

496
00:25:10,421 --> 00:25:13,207
Welcome to the unit,
Agent Van Pelt.

497
00:25:13,294 --> 00:25:16,253
Thank you, agent Rigsby.

498
00:25:16,340 --> 00:25:18,908
[male narrator on TV]
She explodes into action,

499
00:25:18,995 --> 00:25:22,564
reaching up
to 60 miles per hour.

500
00:25:22,651 --> 00:25:26,350
She easily outruns
her terrifying prey.

501
00:25:54,640 --> 00:25:56,772
[panting]

502
00:25:58,469 --> 00:25:59,906
Oh!

503
00:25:59,993 --> 00:26:02,125
[alarm blaring]

504
00:26:21,188 --> 00:26:22,885
"Greetings, old friend.
It's been a while.

505
00:26:22,972 --> 00:26:26,062
"I hope you are keeping well.
I am thriving and happy.

506
00:26:26,149 --> 00:26:29,936
"I have 12 wives now and will
soon begin courting number 13.

507
00:26:30,023 --> 00:26:32,329
"Why can't you catch me?

508
00:26:32,416 --> 00:26:35,506
"You must feel so powerless
and stupid and sad.

509
00:26:35,594 --> 00:26:37,117
"Oh, well.

510
00:26:37,204 --> 00:26:39,641
All the best. Red John."

511
00:26:41,164 --> 00:26:43,123
That sounds like
the real deal to me.

512
00:26:43,210 --> 00:26:44,733
Sounds like Red John.
It's not.

513
00:26:44,820 --> 00:26:47,083
Red John wouldn't risk capture
just to taunt me.

514
00:26:47,170 --> 00:26:49,216
So the real killer's
trying to throw us off-track?

515
00:26:49,303 --> 00:26:52,480
Cho, find out where Price
Randolph was a half an hour ago.

516
00:26:52,567 --> 00:26:54,830
'Rigsby, I want you to check
the hotel security cameras.'

517
00:26:54,917 --> 00:26:56,789
'Get those over to forensics.'

518
00:27:02,403 --> 00:27:03,709
You okay?

519
00:27:03,796 --> 00:27:05,972
Absolutely.

520
00:27:06,059 --> 00:27:07,538
Get some sleep.

521
00:27:15,024 --> 00:27:16,591
[door closes]

522
00:27:36,219 --> 00:27:38,047
[telephone rings]

523
00:27:38,134 --> 00:27:40,180
[ring]

524
00:27:40,267 --> 00:27:42,138
[ring]

525
00:27:42,225 --> 00:27:44,880
[ring]

526
00:27:44,967 --> 00:27:46,447
Hello?

527
00:27:46,534 --> 00:27:49,145
- Good morning.
- You didn't sleep, did you?

528
00:27:49,232 --> 00:27:50,886
[slurping]

529
00:27:54,194 --> 00:27:55,543
Hi. I-I'd like
to make an appointment

530
00:27:55,630 --> 00:27:57,676
with Dr. Wagner, please.
It's urgent.

531
00:27:57,763 --> 00:28:00,113
'Jane. Patrick Jane.'

532
00:28:00,200 --> 00:28:01,767
Yeah, I'll hold.

533
00:28:01,854 --> 00:28:03,769
Forensics maybe got a break.

534
00:28:03,856 --> 00:28:05,422
The blood on the cloth
in the envelope

535
00:28:05,509 --> 00:28:07,250
is Alison Randolph's.

536
00:28:07,337 --> 00:28:10,819
But they found a hair in there..
Doesn't belong to her or Tannen.

537
00:28:10,906 --> 00:28:13,474
Guess who
it doesbelong to.

538
00:28:13,561 --> 00:28:16,999
It's yours, Tag.
Amazing, huh?

539
00:28:20,829 --> 00:28:22,135
Science.

540
00:28:26,835 --> 00:28:28,576
This is insane.

541
00:28:28,663 --> 00:28:29,838
I didn't...

542
00:28:29,925 --> 00:28:31,884
'I didn't kill Alison.'

543
00:28:31,971 --> 00:28:33,624
[Cho]
'How do you explain
your hair in the envelope?'

544
00:28:33,712 --> 00:28:35,539
Either it was a mistake

545
00:28:35,626 --> 00:28:37,672
'or-or I'm being framed.'

546
00:28:37,759 --> 00:28:39,326
'Who would want to frame you?'

547
00:28:39,413 --> 00:28:41,154
'We don't want to, if that's
what you're thinking.'

548
00:28:41,241 --> 00:28:43,373
[whispers]
He and Alison were lovers.

549
00:28:43,460 --> 00:28:45,114
Who would want to
frame you, Tag?

550
00:28:46,681 --> 00:28:48,117
My brother.

551
00:28:48,204 --> 00:28:51,468
[Cho]
'Why would he want
to do that?'

552
00:28:51,555 --> 00:28:53,819
Alison and I were lovers.

553
00:28:55,864 --> 00:28:58,519
I think youarepsychic.
You're just afraid to admit it.

554
00:28:58,606 --> 00:29:00,434
Mm-hmm.

555
00:29:00,521 --> 00:29:02,349
So..

556
00:29:04,090 --> 00:29:05,265
[clears throat]

557
00:29:06,745 --> 00:29:08,181
So..

558
00:29:11,010 --> 00:29:12,838
Why is it
you can't sleep?

559
00:29:12,925 --> 00:29:14,361
Because I can't
get the good pills

560
00:29:14,448 --> 00:29:15,666
without talking to a doctor.

561
00:29:15,754 --> 00:29:17,668
Hmm.

562
00:29:17,756 --> 00:29:19,627
And you don't like
talking to doctors.

563
00:29:19,714 --> 00:29:20,976
Meh, you know,
they always wanna be

564
00:29:21,063 --> 00:29:23,718
the smartest person in the room,
don't they?

565
00:29:23,805 --> 00:29:25,894
When in fact that's me,
obviously.

566
00:29:29,898 --> 00:29:34,816
You protect your core self
very fiercely.

567
00:29:34,903 --> 00:29:36,992
What do you think
is the reason for that?

568
00:29:37,079 --> 00:29:39,125
[chuckles]

569
00:29:39,212 --> 00:29:43,520
You know, this is exactly
how I imagined it would be.

570
00:29:43,607 --> 00:29:45,609
You gonna ask me
about my mother?

571
00:29:45,696 --> 00:29:47,568
Do you want me
to ask you about your mother?

572
00:29:47,655 --> 00:29:48,917
I just wanna sleep.

573
00:29:50,614 --> 00:29:54,575
So what is it
that keeps you awake?

574
00:29:54,662 --> 00:29:56,751
[male #4]
'What's his name?
Red john?'

575
00:29:56,838 --> 00:29:58,579
That's right. Red John.

576
00:29:58,666 --> 00:30:02,235
Uh, he's-he's killed at least
eight women that we know of.

577
00:30:02,322 --> 00:30:04,933
Uh, the police asked me to try
and get a psychic fix on him

578
00:30:05,020 --> 00:30:07,240
to see if I could get
a sense of who this man is.

579
00:30:07,327 --> 00:30:11,200
Uh, how do you do that exactly,
get a psychic fix on someone?

580
00:30:11,287 --> 00:30:13,115
Well, Davis

581
00:30:13,202 --> 00:30:15,204
true demonic evil
burns like fire.

582
00:30:15,291 --> 00:30:19,208
It-it burns with
a terrible cold, dark flame.

583
00:30:19,295 --> 00:30:22,211
I force myself
to look into that flame

584
00:30:22,298 --> 00:30:24,823
and I see an image
of the evildoer..

585
00:30:24,910 --> 00:30:27,086
In this case, Red John.

586
00:30:27,173 --> 00:30:30,350
He's an ugly,
tormented little man.

587
00:30:30,437 --> 00:30:32,178
A lonely soul.

588
00:30:32,265 --> 00:30:35,050
Sad, very sad.

589
00:30:56,071 --> 00:30:59,509
"Dear Mr. Jane, I do not like
to be slandered in the media

590
00:30:59,596 --> 00:31:01,772
"especially by
a dirty money-grubbing fraud.

591
00:31:01,860 --> 00:31:03,339
"if you are a real psychic

592
00:31:03,426 --> 00:31:05,385
"instead of
a dishonest little worm

593
00:31:05,472 --> 00:31:07,387
"you wouldn't need to open
the door to see

594
00:31:07,474 --> 00:31:10,564
what I've done to
your lovely wife and child."

595
00:31:15,656 --> 00:31:18,050
[door creaks]

596
00:31:19,225 --> 00:31:21,053
[Wagner]
'Mr. Jane?'

597
00:31:21,140 --> 00:31:22,881
'Mr. Jane?'

598
00:31:24,926 --> 00:31:27,668
'What is it
that keeps you awake?'

599
00:31:27,755 --> 00:31:29,061
[sighs deeply]

600
00:31:29,148 --> 00:31:30,410
Um.. \

601
00:31:35,894 --> 00:31:38,766
You know, when I was a boy,
we had a farm.

602
00:31:38,853 --> 00:31:40,899
It's a lot of work.

603
00:31:43,162 --> 00:31:45,425
I was kind of a lazy kid.

604
00:31:45,512 --> 00:31:46,643
Yes?

605
00:31:50,909 --> 00:31:52,867
I'd always be trying
to get my little brother Jimmy

606
00:31:52,954 --> 00:31:54,390
to do my Chores for me.

607
00:31:57,567 --> 00:32:01,571
One day, I promised him a dollar
if he'd cut the firewood.

608
00:32:01,658 --> 00:32:02,921
Hmm.

609
00:32:03,008 --> 00:32:04,879
'Well..'

610
00:32:04,966 --> 00:32:07,403
'he opened up an artery
in his leg on the saw'

611
00:32:07,490 --> 00:32:09,405
'and he bled to death..'

612
00:32:11,712 --> 00:32:14,976
...died..

613
00:32:15,063 --> 00:32:17,239
...doing my Chores for me.

614
00:32:23,028 --> 00:32:25,291
You know..

615
00:32:25,378 --> 00:32:27,858
that's almost
exactly the same thing

616
00:32:27,946 --> 00:32:30,513
that happened to Johnny Cash.

617
00:32:30,600 --> 00:32:32,167
Is it really?

618
00:32:33,560 --> 00:32:34,996
'Wow.'

619
00:32:36,432 --> 00:32:37,781
That's spooky.

620
00:32:43,787 --> 00:32:45,180
Mr. Randolph, good--

621
00:32:45,267 --> 00:32:47,182
Cut the crap.
My brother's done nothing.

622
00:32:47,269 --> 00:32:49,010
And you scumbags haven't got
the stones to come after me

623
00:32:49,097 --> 00:32:50,969
so you come after my family.
That is flat-out persecution.

624
00:32:51,056 --> 00:32:52,361
Price, what did we agree?

625
00:32:52,448 --> 00:32:53,710
Mr. Randolph, rest assured,

626
00:32:53,797 --> 00:32:55,016
there's no intent
to persecute you.

627
00:32:55,103 --> 00:32:56,409
We scumbags are holding
your brother

628
00:32:56,496 --> 00:32:57,758
because we have
physical evidence

629
00:32:57,845 --> 00:32:59,542
linking him to the crime
and potential motive

630
00:32:59,629 --> 00:33:01,066
in that he states that
whenever you weren't around

631
00:33:01,153 --> 00:33:03,111
he was banging your wife
like a big bass drum.

632
00:33:03,198 --> 00:33:04,721
[laughs]

633
00:33:04,808 --> 00:33:06,114
Tag and Alison?

634
00:33:09,596 --> 00:33:10,814
That's what he states,
and he further states

635
00:33:10,901 --> 00:33:12,468
that it was you
that killed Alison

636
00:33:12,555 --> 00:33:13,643
'and you're now trying
to frame him in revenge.'

637
00:33:13,730 --> 00:33:16,951
What'd you say? Wh..
Bastard!

638
00:33:17,038 --> 00:33:18,779
[Van Pelt]
'Hey.'

639
00:33:18,866 --> 00:33:21,347
Aah! Son of a bitch!

640
00:33:21,434 --> 00:33:23,566
[Tag]
'You treated her like
trash! What did you expect?'

641
00:33:23,653 --> 00:33:25,133
I didn't expect my little
brother to be banging my wife!

642
00:33:25,220 --> 00:33:27,135
You little punk bastard!

643
00:33:36,492 --> 00:33:40,322
Everything you've told me
is total fiction, isn't it?

644
00:33:40,409 --> 00:33:41,976
Yes.

645
00:33:42,063 --> 00:33:44,152
Why?

646
00:33:44,239 --> 00:33:46,633
I can tell
you're in real pain.

647
00:33:46,720 --> 00:33:49,201
Why not tell the truth?

648
00:33:49,288 --> 00:33:51,159
The truth is mine.

649
00:33:54,815 --> 00:33:57,339
- I hear ya.
- Thank you.

650
00:34:04,868 --> 00:34:08,307
Oh. Yes.

651
00:34:08,394 --> 00:34:11,005
Remember, uh, we were talking
about Tannen the other day

652
00:34:11,092 --> 00:34:13,399
and I asked you if he kept
a diary, and you said he did?

653
00:34:13,486 --> 00:34:15,314
Well, there's no diary
among his effects.

654
00:34:15,401 --> 00:34:17,272
- No.
- I'm sorry, no?

655
00:34:17,359 --> 00:34:18,795
No. You have it wrong.

656
00:34:18,882 --> 00:34:20,928
I-I didn't think
he kept a diary.

657
00:34:21,015 --> 00:34:26,151
Strange. Then it must have been
someone else who told me.

658
00:34:26,238 --> 00:34:28,109
Either that
or I'm going mad.

659
00:34:29,893 --> 00:34:31,939
But I definitely,
100% remember hearing

660
00:34:32,026 --> 00:34:33,767
that Tannen kept a diary.

661
00:34:33,854 --> 00:34:35,290
Well, that is strange

662
00:34:35,377 --> 00:34:37,553
but why does it matter
if he kept a diary?

663
00:34:37,640 --> 00:34:38,859
You're right.
It doesn't matter.

664
00:34:38,946 --> 00:34:40,774
Only I was thinking

665
00:34:40,861 --> 00:34:43,733
why do magicians have
beautiful girl assistants?

666
00:34:43,820 --> 00:34:45,431
Why?

667
00:34:45,518 --> 00:34:47,781
Because they're reliable
distracters of attention.

668
00:34:47,868 --> 00:34:50,305
People will look at a beautiful
girl for a long time

669
00:34:50,392 --> 00:34:52,829
before they look
where they should be looking

670
00:34:52,916 --> 00:34:55,484
if they wanna see
how the trick really works.

671
00:34:55,571 --> 00:34:57,225
[both chuckle]

672
00:34:57,312 --> 00:34:59,445
Anyhow, I'll send over a couple
of forensics guys tomorrow

673
00:34:59,532 --> 00:35:01,795
to search his office
and locate that diary.

674
00:35:01,882 --> 00:35:03,884
Mm, didn't they already
search his office?

675
00:35:03,971 --> 00:35:06,930
Oh, they never do it
thoroughly the first time.

676
00:35:07,017 --> 00:35:09,150
Once more for luck, eh?

677
00:35:09,237 --> 00:35:12,545
It's gotta be there somewhere.
Thanks for everything, doc.

678
00:35:12,632 --> 00:35:14,242
- Goodnight.
- Goodnight.

679
00:35:51,932 --> 00:35:53,934
Lost something?

680
00:35:55,501 --> 00:35:57,677
- How did you get in?
- Door was open.

681
00:35:57,764 --> 00:35:59,722
I think I left my phone
in your office.

682
00:35:59,809 --> 00:36:03,465
- The door wasn't open.
- Must have been. Here I am.

683
00:36:08,818 --> 00:36:10,124
What are you doing?

684
00:36:11,865 --> 00:36:13,519
[sighs]

685
00:36:13,606 --> 00:36:17,044
I confess, the temptation
to play detective

686
00:36:17,131 --> 00:36:19,612
was a little too strong.
I..

687
00:36:19,699 --> 00:36:21,657
I was looking
for that diary.

688
00:36:24,312 --> 00:36:26,140
I got a little
carried away.

689
00:36:26,227 --> 00:36:28,229
No kidding.

690
00:36:28,316 --> 00:36:30,579
No diary?

691
00:36:30,666 --> 00:36:31,972
No diary.

692
00:36:34,104 --> 00:36:36,890
Maybe I should have a gander.
I'm good at finding things.

693
00:36:36,977 --> 00:36:39,371
Be my guest.

694
00:36:47,901 --> 00:36:49,642
Hmm.

695
00:36:57,389 --> 00:36:59,826
Hmm.

696
00:36:59,913 --> 00:37:01,654
Hmm.

697
00:37:05,092 --> 00:37:08,008
Hmm.

698
00:37:19,019 --> 00:37:21,717
[grunts]

699
00:37:24,807 --> 00:37:26,331
[grunts]

700
00:37:28,898 --> 00:37:29,856
[sighs]

701
00:37:42,695 --> 00:37:44,262
Eureka.

702
00:37:49,702 --> 00:37:51,921
Dr. Wagner,
thanks for your help.

703
00:38:01,279 --> 00:38:02,976
Mr. Jane.

704
00:38:03,063 --> 00:38:06,327
Uh, your phone.

705
00:38:06,414 --> 00:38:08,155
Right.

706
00:38:09,852 --> 00:38:11,506
Thanks.

707
00:38:18,165 --> 00:38:21,124
Uh, yeah. Got it.

708
00:38:21,211 --> 00:38:23,388
Silly of me.
Well, good-bye again.

709
00:38:23,475 --> 00:38:24,867
Wait.

710
00:38:27,740 --> 00:38:29,611
Give me the diary.

711
00:38:52,155 --> 00:38:54,593
- It's very amusing.
- I try.

712
00:38:57,813 --> 00:38:59,859
[inhales sharply]

713
00:38:59,946 --> 00:39:04,646
I knew. I knew it might
be a trick, but I..

714
00:39:04,733 --> 00:39:06,648
I had to be sure.

715
00:39:06,735 --> 00:39:10,478
Yes. That's how
the trick works.

716
00:39:10,565 --> 00:39:12,654
What led you to me?

717
00:39:12,741 --> 00:39:15,831
Not that I'm saying I did it.
I'm just asking.

718
00:39:15,918 --> 00:39:19,182
When we first met, you said you
didn't know who Red John was

719
00:39:19,269 --> 00:39:22,447
but you have books
on criminal psychiatry

720
00:39:22,534 --> 00:39:25,450
there..
that have chapters on him.

721
00:39:25,537 --> 00:39:27,016
You're the Randolph
family doctor

722
00:39:27,103 --> 00:39:30,411
so you could easily
get a strand of Tag's hair

723
00:39:30,498 --> 00:39:33,283
and, being a doctor,

724
00:39:33,371 --> 00:39:38,332
you could hack up another human
without difficulty.

725
00:39:38,419 --> 00:39:40,552
It's obvious it was you.

726
00:39:40,639 --> 00:39:44,120
[scoffs]
That's it?

727
00:39:44,207 --> 00:39:46,166
You have nothing.

728
00:39:46,253 --> 00:39:47,950
That's just guesswork.

729
00:39:48,037 --> 00:39:49,778
Oh, I know.

730
00:39:49,865 --> 00:39:52,390
I just wanted to be sure
I had the right answer.

731
00:39:54,304 --> 00:39:56,611
I was surprised.
I gotta be honest.

732
00:39:56,698 --> 00:40:00,093
You don't seem to be
a wicked man.

733
00:40:00,180 --> 00:40:02,269
But you are.

734
00:40:02,356 --> 00:40:04,837
[chuckles]

735
00:40:04,924 --> 00:40:07,013
You're angry
about the letter.

736
00:40:09,232 --> 00:40:11,060
Yeah, it was
a bit mean-spirited.

737
00:40:13,889 --> 00:40:16,152
For the record,
I'm sorry about your family

738
00:40:16,239 --> 00:40:18,720
I can only imagine
your pain.

739
00:40:18,807 --> 00:40:23,029
I'm not...a wicked man.

740
00:40:23,116 --> 00:40:24,422
My conscience is clear.

741
00:40:24,509 --> 00:40:26,032
Really?

742
00:40:26,119 --> 00:40:29,557
Right now in Africa,
there's 3,000 beautiful children

743
00:40:29,644 --> 00:40:33,343
alive today who should be dead,
but they aren't because of me.

744
00:40:35,520 --> 00:40:38,044
Tannen was gonna ruin me

745
00:40:38,131 --> 00:40:40,829
and destroy all that work..

746
00:40:43,658 --> 00:40:45,007
...over nothing.

747
00:40:45,094 --> 00:40:46,531
Money.

748
00:40:46,618 --> 00:40:49,751
"Theft," he called it.

749
00:40:49,838 --> 00:40:51,405
"Embezzlement."

750
00:40:51,492 --> 00:40:55,061
Self-righteous idiot.

751
00:40:55,148 --> 00:40:56,584
It's simple math.

752
00:40:56,671 --> 00:40:58,281
If I go to jail,

753
00:40:58,368 --> 00:41:01,154
thousands of kids will die.

754
00:41:01,241 --> 00:41:04,287
So I made
a rational, moral decision

755
00:41:04,374 --> 00:41:06,899
to kill Tannen..

756
00:41:06,986 --> 00:41:08,204
...for the greater good.

757
00:41:08,291 --> 00:41:11,120
And Alison?
What did she do wrong?

758
00:41:11,207 --> 00:41:12,557
Mm.

759
00:41:12,644 --> 00:41:14,254
[electricity crackles]

760
00:41:14,341 --> 00:41:16,299
As you said, she was
the magician's assistant

761
00:41:16,386 --> 00:41:17,562
just a distraction.

762
00:41:17,649 --> 00:41:18,998
Oh.

763
00:41:19,085 --> 00:41:20,652
If only Tannen died,
the police would've been

764
00:41:20,739 --> 00:41:23,002
all over this place,
wouldn't they?

765
00:41:23,089 --> 00:41:27,136
Truly, is killing two
any worse than killing one,

766
00:41:27,223 --> 00:41:30,444
when so many lives are at stake?
I don't think so.

767
00:41:30,531 --> 00:41:33,273
You poor, sad man.

768
00:41:33,360 --> 00:41:34,492
You're under arrest.
Let's go.

769
00:41:34,579 --> 00:41:36,842
I'm pointing a gun at you.

770
00:41:36,929 --> 00:41:39,018
You really think
I would set you up so nicely

771
00:41:39,105 --> 00:41:40,933
and let you pull
a loaded gun on me?

772
00:41:42,543 --> 00:41:44,284
I took the bullets
out earlier.

773
00:41:44,371 --> 00:41:45,894
[metal clinks]

774
00:41:58,559 --> 00:41:59,865
- You're late!
- What?

775
00:41:59,952 --> 00:42:02,215
- Draw your weapon!
- Huh?

776
00:42:02,302 --> 00:42:03,695
Drop the gun!

777
00:42:03,782 --> 00:42:05,610
'Hands on your head.'

778
00:42:05,697 --> 00:42:09,091
Get down on your knees.
Down.

779
00:42:11,572 --> 00:42:13,400
[gun slides across floor]

780
00:42:15,794 --> 00:42:17,665
[laughs]

781
00:42:17,752 --> 00:42:20,625
[indistinct radio chatter]

782
00:42:24,846 --> 00:42:26,805
Closed case doughnuts
are here.

783
00:42:37,380 --> 00:42:39,208
I just went to get
sleeping pills, I swear to god.

784
00:42:39,295 --> 00:42:41,820
I-I didn't evenwannago.
You know I didn't want to go.

785
00:42:41,907 --> 00:42:43,952
Right.

786
00:42:44,039 --> 00:42:47,173
Yeah, you didn't
set Wagner up..

787
00:42:47,260 --> 00:42:49,218
...didn't figure
it was him days ago.

788
00:42:49,305 --> 00:42:51,133
You didn't let us
tear apart the victim's family

789
00:42:51,220 --> 00:42:53,571
simply to satisfy
your childish need for drama.

790
00:42:53,658 --> 00:42:55,398
Meh, that family
was screwed anyway.

791
00:42:55,485 --> 00:42:57,357
Don't blame yourselves, guys.

792
00:43:07,672 --> 00:43:10,588
[siren wailing in distance]

793
00:43:16,332 --> 00:43:19,422
Don't even start.
I'm still angry.

794
00:43:19,509 --> 00:43:21,729
- I'm sorry.
- No, you're not.

795
00:43:29,171 --> 00:43:30,738
A frog?

796
00:43:30,825 --> 00:43:33,088
Well, this makes everything
better, doesn't it?

797
00:43:34,481 --> 00:43:35,787
[gasps]

798
00:43:52,455 --> 00:43:54,022
[keys drop on table]

799
00:44:14,869 --> 00:44:16,741
[grunts]

800
00:44:24,966 --> 00:44:26,838
[sighs]

